,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.04193159544385301,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":91.9,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02287032589978535,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":36.5,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02316817081025802,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":61.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.00985,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Full Truck Alliance Co. Ltd., together with its subsidiaries, operates a digital freight platform that connects shippers with truckers to facilitate shipments across distance ranges, cargo weights, and types in the People's Republic of China and Hong Kong. The company offers freight matching services, such as freight listing and brokerage services; and transaction services, as well as various value-added services, such as credit solutions, insurance brokerage, software solutions, electronic toll collection, Intelligent Driving Related Services, and energy services. It also provides technology development and other services. Full Truck Alliance Co. Ltd. was founded in 2011 and is based in Guiyang, China.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Hui  Zhang | Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 46","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $227K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, improving at 25%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $82K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["Full Truck Alliance Co. Ltd. is a mid-cap technology business with a $9.6B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +28.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $675M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 36 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.04\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 26% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 59% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 119% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Contrasting Full Truck Alliance (NYSE:YMM) & Werner Enterprises (NASDAQ:WERN)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/contrasting-full-truck-alliance-nyseymm-werner-enterprises-nasdaqwern.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793870965.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(YMM) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/1/YMM_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_110426121002_1793812202.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793812202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Full Truck Alliance (NYSE:YMM) Shares Down 4.5% \u2013 Time to Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/30/full-truck-alliance-nyseymm-shares-down-4-5-time-to-sell.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793366463.0,"